From 23d71fe82d3e172e7100cdc7a75e7723e8e6bb5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skali <you@skali.app>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:32:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): full-screen incoming call banner while app is
 out

Adds a native, phone-style incoming call screen that rings, wakes the
device, and shows over the lock screen even when the app is force-killed.

- New CallMessagingService (extends Capacitor's MessagingService) that
  handles data-only 'incoming_call' FCM messages and posts a CallStyle
  notification with a full-screen intent.
- New IncomingCallActivity shown over the lock screen with Answer /
  Decline. Answer deep-links skali://call?... back into MainActivity.
- New CallActionReceiver handles Decline while the app is out; reads
  auth token + API base from SharedPreferences and POSTs
  /api/call/decline in a background thread.
- Manifest: new permissions (USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT, WAKE_LOCK, VIBRATE,
  DISABLE_KEYGUARD, FOREGROUND_SERVICE, FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MICROPHONE),
  MainActivity gets a skali://call deep-link filter, and our service is
  registered with tools:node='replace' so it wins the manifest merge.
- Backend: new push_call_ring_to_user() helper sends data-only,
  priority=high FCM (ttl=45s, direct_boot_ok). /api/call/ring is
  rewritten to use it; every other push flow is unchanged.
- Web: pushNotifications.ts stashes the current Supabase JWT + API base
  in SharedPreferences (group 'skali_call_prefs') via
  @capacitor/preferences so the native decline receiver can hit the
  backend while the app is out, and routes the skali://call deep link
  into a 'skali:incoming-call-accept' CustomEvent.

Requires: yarn add @capacitor/preferences && yarn cap:sync.
iOS is intentionally out of scope; ship PushKit + CallKit later.
